        "--title",
        "comparison launch",
        "Upgrade the htmlparser2 parser this project's tests build their DOM fixtures with. In package.json the devDependency \"htmlparser2\" is currently \"~11.0.0\"; change it to exactly \"12.0.0\" (declare \"12.0.0\", no range) and regenerate package-lock.json with npm so that the lockfile resolves htmlparser2 to 12.0.0, its root package entry records the same declaration, and npm ci installs 12.0.0. htmlparser2 12 aligns HTML parsing with the WHATWG specification (for example <image> becomes <img> and <iframe> content is raw text); the full check (npm test: vitest, then eslint, tsc and biome) must pass against it. Do not change any other dependency declaration, the scripts block or anything under src; the change is package.json and package-lock.json only.\n\nVisible acceptance check (it must pass; it is not the only criterion): node acceptance/visible/check.mjs\nThe project's own tests run with: npm test\nDo not modify anything under acceptance/visible/."
      ],
